## Recommendations for Wanjiku

1. Wanjiku should increase her stock of tomatoes and sukuma because their current quantities (18 kg and 9 kg respectively) are below their reorder levels.

2. She should focus on improving weekday sales because the average weekend sales of KES 4,900 are 82.50% higher than weekday sales of KES 2,685.

3. She should take advantage of the strong weekend performance, particularly Saturday, which recorded the highest sales of KES 5,600 in Week 2.

4. Wanjiku should monitor her weekly performance because sales increased from KES 22,050 in Week 1 to KES 24,400 in Week 2, representing 10.66% growth.

5. Avocado has the highest gross margin at 42.86%. Wanjiku should monitor its sales demand and profitability when making future stocking decisions.
